{"title":"2017 AIME II Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Abuse_the_discriminant)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Abuse the discriminant)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Squeezing/Sandwich_method)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Squeezing/Sandwich method)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(Using_factors)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (Using factors)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Solution_7_(alternative_factoring)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 7 (alternative factoring)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find the sum of all positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/a/e1a9ea3e8d2a5e5c7899454373b09aadd8be457a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{n^2+85n+2017}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"143\" height=\"18\" /> is an integer.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Manipulating the given expression, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/9/979b95944438936f54a5f39d7f3061b2726ed772.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{n^2+85n+2017}=\\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{4n^2+340n+8068}=\\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{(2n+85)^2+843}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"529\" height=\"37\" />. The expression under the radical must be an square number for the entire expression to be an integer, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/f/62f37a9a87954b60605dff6e95ac4112c2c3e500.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2n+85)^2+843=s^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"170\" height=\"19\" />. Rearranging, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/2/762b733862505f711802dab22b3d4c49d094fb2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s^2-(2n+85)^2=843$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"171\" height=\"19\" />. By difference of squares, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/f/fffaf428a61876582db2242ea54e4682f3ddee69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(s-(2n+85))(s+(2n+85))=1\\times843=3\\times281$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"406\" height=\"20\" />. It is easy to check that those are all the factor pairs of 843. Considering each factor pair separately, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/3/f9369c60cc68095c9905a05f666299a8ad03c635.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2n+85$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"59\" height=\"14\" /> is found to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/2/352084375acbce3724da8cd134342d29c72f1f15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$421$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/f/cdfe592c0de43e99a92604c8da6f92c6708e919d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$139$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />. The two values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> that satisfy one of the equations are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/1/c7116bbc884d2cf49e25754864ae00d9c42d2d90.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$168$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/5/1051e7d41ec0b8bd688a872be17538413f4ee97b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$27$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Summing these together gives us the answer&#160;; <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/f/c7f722a5606b5eaa3887cda9e36e5782859f5932.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$168+27=\\boxed{195}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"131\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Clearly, the result when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is plugged into the given expression is larger than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> itself. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> be the positive difference between that result and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/e/fcecf9901aa7d6bde3c1dd5551301a4a587c8ef8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{n^2+85n+2017}=n+x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"211\" height=\"18\" />. Squaring both sides and canceling the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/0/6006bba637eef443381fbaff768fa62d9ff41e62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"17\" /> terms gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/f/48f7b5dd132fbf73b4345b5100a783dfef7e521d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$85n+2017=2xn+x^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"181\" height=\"16\" />. Combining like terms, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/e/0ee9f74a52984e414ba906dfa60b95e0ec1c07e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(85-2x)n=x^2-2017$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"185\" height=\"19\" />, so\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/e/8fec68806ad2fa564820e73e44e128ac49012d04.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n=\\frac{x^2-2017}{85-2x}.\\]\" width=\"118\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is positive, there are two cases, which are simple (luckily). Remembering that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is a positive integer, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/6/7762a2a1221da88cfa4dc27afd9e4d4c417dac6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2-2017$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"76\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/6/d26a3a5facc129634281b1452904b3284105db9c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$85-2x$\" width=\"59\" height=\"12\" /> are either both positive or both negative. The smallest value for which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/3/c63e6bc41fb67ffc3a785384ba7455c0f5be6398.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2&gt;2017$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"78\" height=\"15\" /> is 45, which makes the denominator, and the entire expression, negative. Evaluating the other case where numerator and denominator are both negative, then we have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/7/a7797737765dc498497015320be287bb55e5ef3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&lt;45$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"55\" height=\"15\" /> (from the numerator) and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/0/2b0a4f30f6a170aebd9d08f160455fa383ef9bc9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$85-2x&lt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"92\" height=\"13\" />, which means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/c/7eca2ff6c9a44a962e958646d0df4b20cbfa742d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&gt;42$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"12\" />. This only gives two solutions, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/4/0045f13d25b7786d584b6ba3749d7691f3ebad83.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=43, 44$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"79\" height=\"16\" />. Plugging these into the expression for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, we find that they result in 27 and 168, which both satisfy the initial question. Therefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/f/c7f722a5606b5eaa3887cda9e36e5782859f5932.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$168+27=\\boxed{195}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"131\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Abuse_the_discriminant.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Abuse_the_discriminant)\">Solution 3 (Abuse the discriminant)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Abuse the discriminant)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the integer given by the square root be represented by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/9/d9937827e152ce7c1a467c755a3e52dd4537bda3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 = n^2 + 85n + 2017 - x^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"200\" height=\"16\" />. For this to have rational solutions for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> (checking whether they are integers is done later), the discriminant of this quadratic must be a perfect square. (This can be easily shown using the quadratic formula.)\n</p><p>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/6/f2688034bdbccb167d000f1c5d2e20b3b18d1721.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b^2 - 4ac = 7225 + 4x^2 - 8068 = y^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"272\" height=\"18\" /> for some integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/6/bc610d3161b6a0f1fd8cea0b5de99d06f0063a93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4x^2 - 843 = y^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"116\" height=\"18\" />. Rearranging this equation yields that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/7/6b7f56f3ed6a8f9b8c3ab6462f25d65abf9eae1f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$843 = (2x+y)(2x-y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"181\" height=\"18\" />. Noticing that there are 2 factor pairs of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/d/42dda8bd65af1f09dc3272f01d963803bfab1488.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$843$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />, namely, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/1/a31b6b75fc5be5cb3a6a82b6f15bbb385424e1f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1*843$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"55\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0ae4bd501bdfd3f4d319d5f3158ef93af688878.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3*281$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"13\" />, there are 2 systems to solve for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> that create rational <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. These yield solutions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/3/e53b1fe25be1c679117fb44a6a886fe1247d189a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x,y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"44\" height=\"20\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/b/75bc62ce17e5e81d3f7f5ad398226d68d0b42d38.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(211, 421)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"75\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/3/a0338b33f540339fba2feeab80f83c48ee4eef3c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(71, 139)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"70\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>The solution to the initial quadratic in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> must then be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/d/b1daf0fb42a3da26df1fc730ed21965799cc4cd1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{-85 \\pm \\sqrt{85^2 - 4(2017 - x^2)}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"222\" height=\"41\" />. Noticing that for each value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> that has rational solutions for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, the corresponding value of the square root of the discriminant is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, the formula can be rewritten as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/c/74cc463d5b41e74893aa6e54eb30274debf4923d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = \\frac{-85 \\pm y}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"101\" height=\"37\" />. One solution is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/6/8e648e7c5425ac7fab4983811a27a1d0169aa1b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{421 - 85}{2} = 168$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"122\" height=\"37\" /> and the other solution is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/9/7e9284c45b127811ff778cabec76d6b2ec8455eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{139 - 85}{2} = 27$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"114\" height=\"37\" />. Thus the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/e/4fe90b4d26970a07591c85c9caa3a5c4971d632e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$168 + 27 = \\boxed{195}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"131\" height=\"23\" /> as both rational solutions are integers.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Squeezing.2FSandwich_method.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Squeezing/Sandwich_method)\">Solution 4 (Squeezing/Sandwich method)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Squeezing/Sandwich method)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/2/db284f4da3fb8570a608bab5ed683e8a686e62de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n+42)^2= n^2+84n+1764$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"225\" height=\"19\" />. Also note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/4/284049a97534b0db6f90e79985798aa2f8ab5640.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n+45)^2= n^2+90n+2025$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"224\" height=\"19\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/c/ecc71dfd853ea365cad1430f8eb2acdd9d2b209a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(n+42)^2&lt; n^2+85n+2017&lt;(n+45)^2\\]\" width=\"319\" height=\"19\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/3/ea38aa970f7d321841b5838f42d3dd02fa2dab6b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2+85n+2017$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"128\" height=\"16\" /> is a perfect square. Hence,<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/7/1e703ea7115c62f2cfedaa54c4282a2abdbf2d88.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n^2+85n+2017= (n+43)^2\\]\" width=\"223\" height=\"19\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/f/03f9970365c3122286a51e0948fe06c5e8155867.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n^2+85n+2017= (n+44)^2.\\]\" width=\"228\" height=\"19\" /> Solving the two equations yields the two solutions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/3/4f32f3be4664708bd8ec43880b9ad1f8c9017a10.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n= 168, 27$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"88\" height=\"16\" />. Therefore, our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/2/302531f850f077001451335ccfdf8d0dcca59f5a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{195}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28Using_factors.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(Using_factors)\">Solution 5 (Using factors)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (Using factors)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the expression be equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />. This expression can be factored into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/1/2e1f9fa462795eb541a0c792ece000098f37fd39.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{(n+44)^2-3n+81}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"174\" height=\"32\" />. Then square both sides, and the expression becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/3/4136038fae094c348100c00334a94f4df216c1a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n+44)^2-3n+81=a^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"195\" height=\"19\" />. We have a difference of two squares. Rearranging, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/1/b41d1de7531e23b58fa8da18e750eabc7a8e4fcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n+44+a)(n+44-a)=3(n-27)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"291\" height=\"18\" />. By inspection, the only possible values for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/c/55c471388938f28af4cf296fa96b416160bc6487.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n+44-a)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"95\" height=\"18\" /> are 0 and 1. When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/2/d722844614a0c79a7df726db91d94845505347a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n+44-a)=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"130\" height=\"18\" />, we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/2/2e2040223202fda6384cd6761fab3c8195fe787e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n-27=0$\" width=\"84\" height=\"12\" />. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/5/1051e7d41ec0b8bd688a872be17538413f4ee97b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$27$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is a solution. When we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/2/e723c00660266f2d496b09211917894c89165791.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n+44-a)=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"129\" height=\"18\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/b/b3bf8a68315704f5115a2f15fdb20f6f51e560e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=a-43$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"84\" height=\"13\" />. Plugging this back to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/c/15c8b61e1a18c40c08b2652a635f5ac84b2a40fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n+44+a)=3(n-27)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"194\" height=\"18\" /> (since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/2/e723c00660266f2d496b09211917894c89165791.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n+44-a)=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"129\" height=\"18\" />), we find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/1/4719485a271e6ee930b1629a1c9e540757e43ab1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=211 \\implies n=168$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"172\" height=\"13\" />. Thus, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/4/3e421cd8cb3fdb2599a5406a0a555009c49919f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$27+168= \\boxed{195}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"131\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p><b>-RootThreeOverTwo</b>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6\">Solution 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Ignore the square root for now. This expression can be factored into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/6/226e32ab17b1f039d907b9211399ced99b4cd208.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n+44)^2-3n+81$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"154\" height=\"19\" />. Just by inspection, when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/a/7da419fbae6e7d19cc3af06fbfe52efd524596d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=27$\" width=\"53\" height=\"12\" />, the expression becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/0/950811e5b467f0749c0f132169cda60207a44bb6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$71^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"24\" height=\"15\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/5/1051e7d41ec0b8bd688a872be17538413f4ee97b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$27$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is a solution. Proceed as Solution 5 to find the other solution(s).\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_7_.28alternative_factoring.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_7_(alternative_factoring)\">Solution 7 (alternative factoring)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 7 (alternative factoring)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>More intuitive, but a little bit slower considering the decimals.\n</p><p><br />\nLabel the entire given expression as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/5/0e5c83cc0c639fc2ed843bbe2d3d209fb478b104.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>Instinctively we can do a crude completion of the square, resulting in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/5/0e5c83cc0c639fc2ed843bbe2d3d209fb478b104.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"17\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/3/893753734ab6005bd94f807019b37be33de113ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n+42.5)^2+210.75$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"159\" height=\"19\" />\nRearrange the equation to get a difference of squares.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/a/27a75f1ff594b12bd3db5df196045063979a1270.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k^2-(n+42.5)^2 = 210.75$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"200\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/c/49cf765165e88c4da420667771a14c739dfdc971.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(k+n+42.5)(k-n-42.5) = 210.75$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"297\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Factor <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/7/0d73f66ebe5a1fab92e69cce3d5b44446964f312.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$21,075$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"53\" height=\"16\" /> to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/e/4ce0583e43880c5a6892f664bd95f9a34b53a5f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^1$\" width=\"14\" height=\"15\" />,<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/9/369aa2b96d08192baf66da44577be596a58d6778.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^2$\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/b/78b6cc87a7cb66c2b9e9c448d27eb5be15c6d8da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$281^1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"32\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>Now the two factors given are either divided by 10 each or one being divided by 100. Let's start with the former case.\n</p><p>If you try <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/a/91a7b680db804d23d299c5ae5b35d1204e8c2e5a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$281*3/10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"80\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/5/915b9123bb652eed0fac426f785667928b1be8ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5*5/10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" />, you quickly realize that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> becomes negative. Naturally, you will realize you want the number's difference to be larger. Try <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/6/ee6ccefc425c1fca267fb65b28c0c527d659802d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$281*5/10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"80\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/3/fb3c2b360e65f0bfe6a79fa3d5ca109da383eb7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3*5/10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" />. This gives an answer of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/5/1051e7d41ec0b8bd688a872be17538413f4ee97b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$27$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />. The next largest possibility also works, giving an <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/1/c7116bbc884d2cf49e25754864ae00d9c42d2d90.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$168$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />. As you rise, some numbers don't work because it results in an n that is not an integer, as in the example of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/4/0c46e18f31c9e1015a7d23234d107f2105060e76.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{281*5*5}{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"82\" height=\"38\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/0/5f0cf2a41ca6fbaafe3d21b823a9bed30c7272fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"20\" height=\"38\" />. \n</p><p>Now if you continue on with the next case, where one factor is divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />, very swiftly will you realize most don't work simply because the difference is too small, or it doesn't give an integer. It helps a lot when you realize that the decimal does not end in a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, the answer will not be an integer. After a few short tests, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/f/c7f722a5606b5eaa3887cda9e36e5782859f5932.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$168+27=\\boxed{195}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"131\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p>-jackshi2006\n- minor latex edits by jske25\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/Z23Yz05eblY\">https://youtu.be/Z23Yz05eblY</a>\n</p>\n<h1><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h1>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II\" title=\"2017 AIME II\">2017 AIME II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems\" title=\"2017 AIME II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2017 AIME II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2017\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2017 AIME II Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2017 AIME II Problems/Problem 7\">Problem 7</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2017 AIME II Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2017 AIME II Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2017 AIME II Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2017 AIME II Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2017 AIME II Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2017 AIME II Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2017 AIME II Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2017 AIME II Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2017 AIME II Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2017 AIME II Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2017 AIME II Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2017 AIME II Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2017 AIME II Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2017 AIME II Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017205021\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.053 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.072 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 631/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1806/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 128/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 19200/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.601      1 -total\n 60.06%    8.169      1 Template:AIME_box\n 38.22%    5.199      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:15517:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017205021 and revision id 221548. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}